   "source_type": "company_pr",
   "_origin": "harvest"
  },
  {
   "event_id": "PSE:SMPH-harvest-5",
   "text": "On February 4, 2002, the LLDA inspected wastewater discharged by SM City Manila, operated by SM Prime Holdings, and laboratory tests revealed that effluent samples failed to conform to inland water standards prescribed by law.",
   "published_at": "2002-02-04",
   "source_url": "https://angkaalaman.com/buod/public-hearing-committee-of-the-llda-vs-sm-prime-holdings-inc-2010-09-22/",
   "source_type": "company_pr",
   "_origin": "harvest"
  },
  {
   "event_id": "PSE:SMPH-harvest-6",
   "text": "On March 12, 2002, the LLDA directed SM Prime Holdings to perform corrective measures to control the pollution and to pay P1,000 per day for discharging pollutive wastewater as a penalty for the violation.",
